  "question": {
    "text": "A ball falls freely from a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. When the ball is at a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, it explodes into two equal pieces. One of them acquires an additional horizontal component of velocity equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, while its vertical component remains the same. The distance between the two pieces when both strike the ground is",
